      "claim": "The serious bodily and mental harm inflicted on Croat civilians (torture, rape, mutilation) satisfies the actus reus element of genocide under Article II(b) of the Genocide Convention.",
      "reasoning": "Article II(b) defines genocide to include \"Causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group;\". Evidence shows Croats were subjected to torture, sexual violence, and other forms of severe injury in detention facilities such as Knin and during the siege of Vukovar. These acts constitute the required serious bodily or mental harm to members of the Croat group.",
